.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-payload 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-payload \- Read a hook payload from stdin
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten payload\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a hook payload from stdin
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-payload\-field(1)
Print one field of a hook payload read from stdin, for a shell hook that must not depend on jq
.TP
batten\-payload\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
